  "rules": [
    "CATIA is always authoritative for engineering knowledge.",
    "The temporary shadow model may supplement CATIA only when required information is unavailable in CATIA.",
    "Committed repository content is authoritative for implementation state.",
    "Local uncommitted changes are not authoritative implementation state.",
    "Every ingested source shall be assigned to exactly one project.",
    "Project identity and source identity shall remain separate.",
    "Framework assignments shall reference valid mapping-target node IDs.",
    "Unknown framework or ontology reference IDs shall be rejected.",
    "Context-only sources shall not create engineering evidence.",
    "Consensus, confidence and variance shall not authorize publication.",
    "Every publication target shall require an exact Human Review Decision.",
    "Required LLM context shall never be silently truncated.",
    "External ontology systems are references and shall not override project engineering authority.",
    "Implementation evidence shall not silently create normative requirements.",
    "The Post-Phase-P Reconciliation Gate shall perform the first Architecture-to-Requirements Reconciliation against CATIA.",
    "Phase Q shall document every accepted architecture decision.",
    "After every SSOT UPDATE, repository synchronization shall be committed, pushed and verified.",
    "Published P9 run artifacts are Processing evidence, not Approved Input.",
    "A P9 run ending in awaiting_review requests Human Review but does not approve engineering knowledge.",
    "Phase G remains planned but shall not begin before completion of the Post-Phase-P Reconciliation Gate and explicit next-phase selection.",
    "The thesis Development Plan shall remain separate from the runtime feature overview.",
    "The completed Phase F/P prototype baseline shall be preserved for presentation during the Post-Phase-P Reconciliation Gate.",
    "Every relevant Phase F/P capability shall be mapped to CATIA requirements or explicitly marked as missing, outdated or conflicting.",
    "The Feature and Requirement Coverage Matrix shall distinguish implemented capability status from authoritative requirement coverage.",
    "Phase N shall retain Shadow-model Migration and final whole-system reconciliation after later implementation phases."
  ],
